s  lush and beautiful which it does but if  you put it up on in a cinema environment  and set of speakers it actually doesn't  sound as great as you would hope it  would so you've got to kind of do a  remastering process but if there's ever  a movie that you're not constantly  tapping your toes - its baby driver  because it's just a great selection a  wide selection of you know great music I  always wanted to get and get into sound  I am from having a Sony cassette walkman  and listening to it in bed and go to  sleep listening to music I used to tape  the top 40 with Tommy Vance on Radio 1  and do kind of pause button editing and  then I saw a documentary which was Ben  Burtt on Star Wars explaining how he  came up with the sounds of the TIE  fighters and she back her and the  blasters and so I knew I wanted to get  into sound and I studied at the school  of audio engineering for a year because  I thought I wanted to get into music  production and I kind of fell in to the  TV and and film side so which I'm glad  for for obvious reasons but yeah  perseverance working hard and treating  people with respect around you and who  work for you I've never been on set I  think I've been on set once in my 25  years of doing this I get involved with  questions and information and you know  because producer would call me to say  we're doing this set up tomorrow how  would you like it but I never go on set  which is a shame because it's there's  that's one end of the spectrum and I'm  this end of the spectrum and never the  twain shall meet but I started off doing  TV stuff and things like spooks for  kudos and life on Mars we did when I had  my company and then I used to split  between doing TV and feature films and  then 10 11 years ago I decided to  concentrate purely on feature films so  that's what I do now movies I would  definitely give a direct message to  anybody who's looking to chase their  dreams I am the embodiment that you can  do it I  I'm from a very small town in Suffolk  and when I went to see my careers  officer and they said tell me anything  you want to do and I'll try and make it  work and I said I want to get into sound  and he said well that's great he said  but I can offer you a job at the local  bank if you liked this work experience  and I decided I didn't want to do that  and I just wanted to push through so  keep out at key tipping away  everything's possible it's a little bit  of luck it's talent and it is it just  don't stop chasing your dreams  you
 

